	(text_box "Signal flows left to right.  Blue boxes: what is on the wire beside them (frequency | level |\nbandwidth | DC), computed by sim/budget.py for the 10 m bench link with 2 dBi whips (the DSA then at\n5.25 dB, holding the demodulator at -20 dBm); the same numbers as docs/images/block_*.svg.  The DSA\nholds the demodulator at about -20 dBm from 3 m to 3 km." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.3200 24.1300 0) (size 91.4400 10.1600)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "eafe0f03-55da-8f48-d880-f73b5cd7d90c"))
	(text_box "RX ANT, 50 ohm SMA: 5.8 GHz\n(4.9-5.9 in spec) | -53.9 dBm\n(1 mV p-p) at 10 m with whips,\n-49.4 dBm (2 mV p-p) at 300 m\nwith panels | a CW line; a\nflip adds +-100 MHz skirts |\nno DC (1.5 pF block) | ABS MAX\n+1 dBm (the LNA).  With the\nSAW filter + LNA module, 5.8\nGHz version (15 dB assumed)\nahead, keep ITS input under\n-14 dBm" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 10.1600 80.0100 0) (size 31.7500 22.8600)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 214 236 255 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "8329f874-d0cb-e10a-bc74-42e0a53a0794"))
	(text_box "SKY65404-31: 13 dB, NF 1.0 dB, 10\nmA.  Skyworks' circuit: 0.5 pF shunt\nat RF_IN, 0.6 nH + 100 nF on VCC,\n100 ohm on the enable." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4000 102.8700 0) (size 34.2900 10.1600)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "79826b08-4eee-9324-3267-0652088399c3"))
	(text_box "after the LNA: -40.9\ndBm (6 mV p-p) |\nnoise -92.0 dBm in\n100 MHz (NF 2.0 dB):\nSNR 38 dB | DC\nblocked" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 48.2600 82.5500 0) (size 21.5900 12.7000)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 214 236 255 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "0ddfc123-7690-002b-104b-dc292b0b4171"))
	(text_box "PE43711: 0-31.75 dB in 0.25 dB\nsteps, serial mode (P/S high; the\nparallel pins grounded as the\ndatasheet asks).  Powers up at 31.75\ndB." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 77.4700 106.6800 0) (size 34.2900 11.4300)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "257c2e4b-9601-02ee-f0c2-a53666dee1f8"))
	(text_box "5.8 GHz (4.9-5.9 in\nspec) | -48.5 dBm (2\nmV p-p) with the DSA\nat 5.25 dB (its\nrange: 0 to 31.75\ndB; it holds the\ndemodulator at -20\ndBm from 3 m to\nabout 300 m) | no DC" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 120.6500 71.1200 0) (size 21.5900 17.7800)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 214 236 255 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "c38ac03a-5583-853b-333e-a5e1133930a9"))
	(text_box "2 x ADL5611: +14.3 dB each at\n5.8 GHz (22 dB at 1 GHz), 5 V\nthrough 43 nH chokes (Table\n6).  The second one (Response\n6) puts the comparators' 20 mV\nfloor near the noise: the fast\npath reads to -81 dBm, the\nslow one to -95." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 139.7000 91.4400 0) (size 30.4800 16.5100)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "aef59592-100a-c773-068f-2afb3ca0a8e0"))
	(text_box "5.8 GHz (4.9-5.9\nin spec) | -34.2\ndBm (12 mV p-p)\nafter the first\ngain block (+14.3\ndB) | DC: 5 V bias\nbehind 43 nH,\nblocked" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 157.4800 26.6700 0) (size 19.0500 16.5100)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 214 236 255 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "8cf815f2-9370-c625-3336-99a1a9d026ec"))
	(text_box "-20 dB coupled-line coupler,\ncopper on the board (7.3 mm\nbeside the line): RX MON on\nthe coupled end (RX MON: -39.9\ndBm (6 mV p-p) at 10 m (-20 dB\nafter the gain blocks)), 49.9\nohm on the isolated end" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 270.5100 76.2000 0) (size 33.0200 15.2400)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "ebab0f87-b42b-6ab7-56f5-35235398f828"))
	(text_box "5.8 GHz (4.9-5.9 in\nspec) | -19.9 dBm\n(64 mV p-p) into the\ndemodulator after\nthe second gain\nblock (IP1dB +8.2:\n28 dB of headroom) |\nDC: 5 V bias behind\n43 nH, blocked" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 280.6700 31.7500 0) (size 21.5900 17.7800)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 214 236 255 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "2920de7a-53cd-aad9-bdeb-7a82fc138003"))
	(text_box "TDK HHM1907B1 1:1 balun,\n4.9-5.95 GHz, 0.8 dB: the\nADL5380 sheet's Johanson\n5400 from JLCPCB's shelf\n(same ratio and band).\nThe 1.5 pF blocks: the RF\nport is AC-coupled (the\nsheet's C2x/C3x); the\nbalun's balanced terminals\nhave a DC path to ground." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 276.8600 91.4400 0) (size 25.4000 20.3200)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "6e2ef526-ef57-57ba-dbb4-921ba58352ba"))
	(text_box "ADL5380: ADJ open at 5.8 GHz (its spec\ncondition): baseband common mode 3.2 V, gain\nx1.95, 390 MHz.  Fit 1.5k here to drop the\ncommon mode to 2.5 V (and the 5.8 GHz gain).\nLO 0 dBm, differential from the synthesizer\nbelow.  JLCPCB C579152; consigned from Digi-\nKey only if their shelf is short on the day." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 336.5500 116.8400 0) (size 43.1800 15.2400)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "8a3faf11-b26a-a9d2-c988-f2d8bfd11ff3"))
	(text_box "LO 5.8 GHz = 232 x 25 MHz\n| 0 dBm differential (316\nmV p-p each side, 27 nH to\n3.3 V, 1.5 pF blocks) |\nmoves with VC: +-580 kHz" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 302.2600 107.9500 0) (size 27.9400 11.4300)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 214 236 255 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "01f51ec7-5ee0-065d-71e3-c9cf2d5b918b"))
	(text_box "THS4541, the FAST arm: gain 4 (Rf\n4.02k / Rg 1k), on 3.3 V.  The 1k\nshunts hold the summing nodes at 1.9 V\n(the demodulator's outputs sit at up\nto 3.8 V; the amplifier's inputs may\nreach 2.0 V).  Noise gain 9.0: 94 MHz,\n3.7 ns rise.  I is the data, inverted:\nILO drives + (the board's pin order;\nthe idle sets the sign).  I_SUM goes\nto sheet 6, where DAC2's channel D\ntrims this arm's offset through 100 k:\na few mV of demodulator offset x4 is a\nfair part of the comparator's 20 mV." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 458.4700 74.9300 0) (size 36.8300 25.4000)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "6d35934b-3cda-a6d0-19ad-2452da62d22e"))
	(text_box "I and Q, differential\npairs | 44 mV rms (124 mV\np-p) at the regulated\nlevel | DC-390 MHz |\ncommon mode 3.8 V, 25 ohm\nper pin | idle: I = +A, Q\n= 0" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 383.5400 26.6700 0) (size 27.9400 15.2400)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 214 236 255 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "43edfdae-87e2-46e7-98cd-09f44aa4cb80"))
	(text_box "THS4541, the FAST arm: gain 4 (Rf\n4.02k / Rg 1k), on 3.3 V.  The 1k\nshunts hold the summing nodes at 1.9 V\n(the demodulator's outputs sit at up\nto 3.8 V; the amplifier's inputs may\nreach 2.0 V).  Noise gain 9.0: 94 MHz,\n3.7 ns rise.  Q is the phase error;\nboth pairs also leave to the slow path\n(sheet 6) and the window comparators\n(sheet 7).  Q_OFF_F (DAC1 C, 100 k)\ntrims this arm's offset: with a weak\npilot the loop's lock point moves by\nthe arm's offset over the pilot's\nslope (PLAN.md section 18)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 377.1900 148.5900 0) (size 36.8300 26.6700)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "793d9568-305b-e34e-b40b-e0690ec13f90"))
	(text_box "CMP I MON: the\ncomparator's output, /10\ninto 50 ohm" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 541.0200 81.2800 0) (size 24.1300 7.6200)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "749e72a0-7b4a-d1e0-d69e-6f63edfaccd9"))
	(text_box "CMP_I, the fast flag: 0 / 3.3 V\nCMOS, 2.5 ns after the input\ncrosses | through 33 ohm (+200 ohm\non the PYNQ) | flips with the\ncarrier's 180 deg | 15.0 ns jack-\nto-register on the PYNQ, 10.6 on\nthe Icepi | confirmed or vetoed by\nCMP_I_S 37 ns later (sheet 6)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 523.2400 43.1800 0) (size 35.5600 16.5100)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 214 236 255 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "c7b5f341-eee8-298a-03da-42921caf4e1f"))
	(text_box "I_P / I_N, the FAST\narm: gain 4, 100 MHz\n(3.5 ns rise) | +-249\nmV peak at the\nregulated level |\ncentred 1.65 V | reads\ndown to -81 dBm at the\nantenna (the\ncomparator floor;\nnoise-quiet would be\n-84) | the data:\nsign(I)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 496.5700 80.0100 0) (size 24.1300 22.8600)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 214 236 255 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "7028ec2c-8118-7d7d-cfca-3a0c38061abe"))
	(text_box "I MON: the fast I arm's\n+ output through 1k:\n1.65 V +-249 mV peak at\nthe regulated level, 100\nMHz.  A high-impedance\nprobe; a 50 ohm input\nreads it /21." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 496.5700 30.4800 0) (size 25.4000 15.2400)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "5956077b-8896-78f6-141e-455a50e9c9d1"))
	(text_box "Q MON: the fast Q arm's\n+ output through 1k:\n1.65 V, 0 at lock, +-249\nmV off lock or during a\nQPSK symbol." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 499.1100 109.2200 0) (size 24.1300 11.4300)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "4ff1e8c9-e193-0679-5c70-5a194bf298ca"))
	(text_box "Q_P / Q_N, the\nFAST arm: the\nphase error, 0 at\nlock, +-249 mV\npeak off lock |\nDC-100 MHz |\ncentred 1.65 V | a\nQPSK symbol puts\n+-176 mV on it" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 481.3300 128.2700 0) (size 19.0500 17.7800)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 214 236 255 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "4805fe8a-5ebf-4a6d-305e-388379f474f0"))
	(text_box "JP101 / JP102 SIGN: set\nthem OPPOSITE ways.\nDefault: JP101 right (Q-\nto B1), JP102 left (Q+ to\nB2): the switch connects A\nto B1 when S is low and to\nB2 when S is high (its\ndatasheet), so ERR =\nsign(I) x Q.  Both the\nother way = -sign(I) x Q:\nmove both if the loop runs\naway (positive feedback)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 345.4400 205.7400 0) (size 26.6700 22.8600)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "4e461ee8-786c-3c27-2376-5741730954c7"))
	(text_box "JP103 SEL: COSTAS = sign(I)\nfrom U107 (the net CMP_I);\nFPGA = LOOP_SEL (hold it high\nfor a plain PLL on Q)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 392.4300 242.5700 0) (size 29.2100 10.1600)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "3d41cf0a-6935-70f1-caba-34afa028a804"))
	(text_box "ERR = sign(I) x Q:\n0 V (about 1.65 V)\nat lock, +-249 mV\npeak off lock |\nDC-100 MHz before\nthe filter | K_d\n0.12 V/rad at the\nregulated level" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 427.9900 213.3600 0) (size 19.0500 16.5100)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 214 236 255 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "1a7546b5-06ff-9655-13bd-858398b87160"))
	(text_box "ERR MON: the loop error\nsign(I) x Q through 1k:\n1.65 V at lock, +-249 mV\noff lock." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 463.5500 193.0400 0) (size 25.4000 10.1600)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "9f06fe5b-661c-3fa5-b3e2-23e1fbcc2396"))
	(text_box "LOOP_HOLD high ties the\nintegrator's input to\nV_MID: no error in, VC\nholds, and the switch's\nleakage goes into V_MID,\nnot the integrator." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 439.4200 241.3000 0) (size 24.1300 12.7000)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "90fd7ba4-e316-5977-3c4b-27ff1e81da1d"))
	(text_box "PI loop filter (sim/budget.py section\n6): R1 10k, R2 750R, C 100 nF C0G -> fn\n3 kHz, zeta 0.7 at the DSA's regulated\nlevel (Kd 0.12 V/rad; it scales with the\nsignal, which the DSA keeps).  U112A\ninverts; U112B inverts again: net non-\ninverting." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 431.8000 160.0200 0) (size 39.3700 15.2400)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "5cdd55c2-950a-935a-c708-9dc236c52c86"))
	(text_box "VC MON. VC: 0.3-3.0 V,\n1.65 V = VCXO centre |\nslow: the 3000 Hz loop | =\n430 kHz/V of LO (x232) |\nV_MID: 1.65 V DC (10k/10k\nfrom 3.3 V, 1 uF): the\nloop's zero" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 553.7200 176.5300 0) (size 26.6700 15.2400)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 214 236 255 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "14ef6f7a-27f9-274a-90e5-e1cd8a008c9b"))
	(text_box "OPA2388: zero drift, 5 uV\noffset, rail-to-rail in and\nout on 3.3 V, so the loop's\nstatic phase error is the\ncomparator's, not the op\namp's.  (The OPA2187 first\ndrawn here needs 4.5 V and\nits inputs stop 2 V below\nthe rail: it could never\nhave sat at 1.65 V on 3.3\nV.)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 539.7500 259.0800 0) (size 26.6700 21.5900)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "92dac75d-eb8b-0942-6b12-dc39b2a85606"))
	(text_box "25 MHz VCXO (SX3V): +-100 ppm\nover 0.3-3.0 V = +-580 kHz at\n5.8 GHz, 15 kHz modulation\nbandwidth.  The loop's VCO.\nSame pads as the TX TCXO." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 41.9100 302.2600 0) (size 31.7500 11.4300)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "bc4d24ae-8b3e-568b-9b05-3aeb386d9c8a"))
	(text_box "25 MHz, 3.3 V\nCMOS square |\n+-100 ppm over\n0.3-3.0 V |\nthrough 100 nF\ninto REF_IN (0.7\nV p-p min)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 97.7900 299.7200 0) (size 17.7800 15.2400)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 214 236 255 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "ab1e8b9b-353c-44fd-14be-59a719839dfa"))
	(text_box "REF OUT: 25 MHz, 3.3 V\nCMOS through 33 ohm |\n1.6 V p-p into 50 ohm,\n3.3 V open | for the TX\nsheet's REF IN\n(transponder).  An MMCX-\nto-SMA lead to the TX\nsheet's REF IN (JP201 to\nREF IN) locks our\ncarrier to the one we\nreceive: the one-antenna\nT/R mode needs it (sheet\n5)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 90.1700 332.7400 0) (size 25.4000 25.4000)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "c1c4f56c-2ca2-00d7-0508-138c49a2730c"))
	(text_box "Loop filter: 80 kHz, 50 deg,\nIcp 2.56 mA (RSET 5.1k, CP =\n7), Kvco 60 MHz/V, N = 232\n(sim/budget.py section 8).\nC0G." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 120.6500 340.3600 0) (size 27.9400 11.4300)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "d98760a8-089c-f319-3075-e1ae4aa0a07d"))
	(text_box "LO RX MON: the\nsynthesizer's second\noutput; enable it in\nsoftware to look at the LO\n(-4 to +5 dBm)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 260.3500 313.6900 0) (size 25.4000 11.4300)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "0bf73bb2-13f1-e29d-7541-41324c86024c"))
	(text_box "RX synthesizer: MAX2871, 5.8 GHz integer-N from the\n25 MHz VCXO (N = 232), RFOUTA differential into the\nADL5380's LO (0 dBm), RFOUTB to the LO RX MON jack.\nIts own LDO, +3V3_PLL_RX.  The Costas loop steers\nthe VCXO, so this whole synthesizer is the loop's\nVCO." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 100.3300 274.3200 0) (size 49.5300 12.7000)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "9f166536-89fa-34b5-fbfb-551f941c54e6"))
	(text_box "VC_OFF: DC from the DAC, 1.65\nV = no offset; +-1 V = -+430\nkHz of LO (acquisition sweep)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 469.9000 311.1500 0) (size 30.4800 7.6200)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 214 236 255 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "90f0e991-1143-7326-8377-c7622faacb57"))
	(text_box "DAC outputs, DC, 0-3.3 V (12\nbit, 0.8 mV): VR_I / VR_Q 0.21\nV (the ladders' centre; also\nthe carrier null) | Q_OFF_F\n(the fast Q arm's offset, +-66\nmV at its output through 100k)\n| VC_OFF 1.65 V" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 483.8700 259.0800 0) (size 29.2100 15.2400)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 214 236 255 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "06cfaa64-788a-b676-3642-1a49a524bde9"))
	(text_box "ADC inputs: I_P, Q_P, VC, ERR\nthrough 10k / 100 nF (160 Hz):\naverages, 0-3.3 V" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 471.1700 345.4400 0) (size 30.4800 7.6200)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 214 236 255 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "512db080-41f0-38eb-492f-dbcb171668ee"))
	(text_box "MCP4728 (I2C 0x60): A = VR_I, B =\nVR_Q (the TX ladders' references,\n0.21 V: amplitude and carrier null),\nC = Q_OFF_F (the fast Q arm's offset\ntrim, through 100 k), D = VC_OFF (a\nfrequency offset / acquisition\nsweep)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 403.8600 299.7200 0) (size 34.2900 15.2400)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "30b05004-dcd7-02be-1247-7c749f72a43f"))
	(text_box "ADS1115 (I2C 0x48, 860 SPS): the\naveraged I and Q (lock = I large, Q\nsmall), VC (how far the VCXO is\npulled) and the loop error.  Its\nfour inputs are the nets named at\nthe taps above (I_P, Q_P, VC, ERR)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 469.9000 320.0400 0) (size 33.0200 12.7000)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "0e4fb7b1-c78e-b346-9d89-504ffc39a4bf"))
